            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Ashley Schulte"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was good. I like the eel sauce at my local sushi bar, it is thicker than this recipe, so I added 2 tablespoons of cornstarch to thicken it up a bit. It was perfect."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jenny"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I took some of the suggestions from other reviewers. I added 1/4 c. low sodium soy sauce, 1/4 c. reg. soy sauce, 1/2 c white sugar, 1/2 c. mirin, 1/4 tsp dashin, 1tsp corn starch. It turned out great!",
            "datePublished": "2010-05-24T15:37:21.340Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "RawWarrior"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Tried it the way the recipe directed and was very good. \nAlso made a batch with ~literally~ some BBQd Unagi blended in it with a bit of cornstarch. Then strained/squeezed through fine cloth. Amazing.",
            "datePublished": "2015-09-15T18:42:32.777Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tim Otey"
            },
            "reviewBody": "So, I didnt have mirin, so I made that (1/2 cup sugar, 1/2 cup water, 4tsp rice vinegar, pinch salt) then used this recipie to make the sauce... simmered it a bit longer and got it thicker that way... turned out a touch sweet, but went great with the crab/cucumber/asparagus/cucumber rolls I made before I realized I was out of Unagi",
            "datePublished": "2018-07-17T21:59:44.430Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "staceysica"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I cooked it on medium heat and let it boil for several minutes to cook down the liquid. It became foamy and started to smell like it was beginning to burn. It didn’t look or smell right. I started again-this time I let it just simmer, not boil, and cooked it for 45 minutes and it turned out perfect. Simmering is the key to a good result!",
            "datePublished": "2018-06-09T00:04:38.773Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "karcar68"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Found that cornstarch isn't necessary to thicken as other reviewers noted...just let it cook long enough and it thickens up quite nicely -- and then more so as it cools. Fantastic flavor, made the poke bowls I used it in delicious!!",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-22T04:45:02.947Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Love, April"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I just made this, and it was delicious! I did not have mirin, so I used marsala instead. I also added some corn starch to thicken a bit. Came out just like my favorite sushi restaurant. I used this on Panko fried chicken. Delish!",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-09T23:01:01.150Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "FairUbe9226"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've just made this and it's really thick so I'm wondering if the people that said it was thin had the heat turned up enough? Mine was really bubbly and went a light shade of brown, once it cooled it was so thick I've had to add more soy sauce. Will try taste test tomorrow when I make sushi....",
            "datePublished": "2023-04-14T17:38:22.251Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GlitzyZest5047"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Made this tonight...absolutely delicious. Followed the recipe exactly and came out perfectly. Definitely needs to be allowed to thicken up while cooling...put it in the refrigerator and it is just the right consistency.",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-27T02:34:00.651Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ToughTofu7391"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great simple tasty sauce. Too thin: You didn't cook it long enough. When it starts getting lots of bubbles, you are almost there. Too thick: You cooked it too long. It will thicken up more as it cools.",
            "datePublished": "2023-06-19T03:13:02.458Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Heath"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This turned out great! I didn't have any Japanese sweet wine so I used a Chardonnay I had in the fridge haha! It it will turned out pretty darn good. The reviewers that said it wasn't thick enough didn't let it cook long enough... you need to boil it until it's the texture you like!",
            "datePublished": "2017-01-26T02:47:58.477Z"
          },
